1	# Tool use with Live API
2	
3	Tool use allows Live API to go beyond just conversation by enabling it to
4	perform actions in the real-world and pull in external context while maintaining
5	a real time connection.
6	You can define tools such as [Function calling](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/function-calling)
7	and [Google Search](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/grounding) with the Live API.
8	
9	## Overview of supported tools
10	
11	Here's a brief overview of the available tools for Live API models:
12	
13	| Tool | Gemini 3.1 Flash Live Preview | Gemini 2.5 Flash Live Preview |
14	|---|---|---|
15	| **Search** | Supported | Supported |
16	| **Function calling** | Supported (synchronous only) | Supported (synchronous and [asynchronous](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/live-api/tools#async-function-calling)) |
17	| **Google Maps** | Not supported | Not supported |
18	| **Code execution** | Not supported | Not supported |
19	| **URL context** | Not supported | Not supported |
20	
21	## Function calling
22	
23	Live API supports function calling, just like regular content generation
24	requests. Function calling lets the Live API interact with external data and
25	programs, greatly increasing what your applications can accomplish.
26	
27	You can define function declarations as part of the session configuration.
28	After receiving tool calls, the client should respond with a list of
29	`FunctionResponse` objects using the `session.send_tool_response` method.
30	
31	See the [Function calling tutorial](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/function-calling) to learn
32	more.
33	
34	> [!NOTE]
35	> **Note:** Unlike the `generateContent` API, the Live API doesn't support automatic tool response handling. You must handle tool responses manually in your client code.
36	
37	### Python
38	
39	    import asyncio
40	    import wave
41	    from google import genai
42	    from google.genai import types
43	
44	    client = genai.Client()
45	
46	    model = "gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview"
47	
48	    # Simple function definitions
49	    turn_on_the_lights = {"name": "turn_on_the_lights"}
50	    turn_off_the_lights = {"name": "turn_off_the_lights"}
51	
52	    tools = [{"function_declarations": [turn_on_the_lights, turn_off_the_lights]}]
53	    config = {"response_modalities": ["AUDIO"], "tools": tools}
54	
55	    async def main():
56	        async with client.aio.live.connect(model=model, config=config) as session:
57	            prompt = "Turn on the lights please"
58	            await session.send_client_content(turns={"parts": [{"text": prompt}]})
59	
60	            wf = wave.open("audio.wav", "wb")
61	            wf.setnchannels(1)
62	            wf.setsampwidth(2)
63	            wf.setframerate(24000)  # Output is 24kHz
64	
65	            async for response in session.receive():
66	                if response.data is not None:
67	                    wf.writeframes(response.data)
68	                elif response.tool_call:
69	                    print("The tool was called")
70	                    function_responses = []
71	                    for fc in response.tool_call.function_calls:
72	                        function_response = types.FunctionResponse(
73	                            id=fc.id,
74	                            name=fc.name,
75	                            response={ "result": "ok" } # simple, hard-coded function response
76	                        )
77	                        function_responses.append(function_response)
78	
79	                    await session.send_tool_response(function_responses=function_responses)
80	
81	            wf.close()
82	
83	    if __name__ == "__main__":
84	        asyncio.run(main())
85	
86	### JavaScript
87	
88	    import { GoogleGenAI, Modality } from '@google/genai';
89	    import * as fs from "node:fs";
90	    import pkg from 'wavefile';  // npm install wavefile
91	    const { WaveFile } = pkg;
92	
93	    const ai = new GoogleGenAI({});
94	    const model = 'gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview';
95	
96	    // Simple function definitions
97	    const turn_on_the_lights = { name: "turn_on_the_lights" } // , description: '...', parameters: { ... }
98	    const turn_off_the_lights = { name: "turn_off_the_lights" }
99	
100	    const tools = [{ functionDeclarations: [turn_on_the_lights, turn_off_the_lights] }]
101	
102	    const config = {
103	      responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO],
104	      tools: tools
105	    }
106	
107	    async function live() {
108	      const responseQueue = [];
109	
110	      async function waitMessage() {
111	        let done = false;
112	        let message = undefined;
113	        while (!done) {
114	          message = responseQueue.shift();
115	          if (message) {
116	            done = true;
117	          } else {
118	            await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
119	          }
120	        }
121	        return message;
122	      }
123	
124	      async function handleTurn() {
125	        const turns = [];
126	        let done = false;
127	        while (!done) {
128	          const message = await waitMessage();
129	          turns.push(message);
130	          if (message.serverContent && message.serverContent.turnComplete) {
131	            done = true;
132	          } else if (message.toolCall) {
133	            done = true;
134	          }
135	        }
136	        return turns;
137	      }
138	
139	      const session = await ai.live.connect({
140	        model: model,
141	        callbacks: {
142	          onopen: function () {
143	            console.debug('Opened');
144	          },
145	          onmessage: function (message) {
146	            responseQueue.push(message);
147	          },
148	          onerror: function (e) {
149	            console.debug('Error:', e.message);
150	          },
151	          onclose: function (e) {
152	            console.debug('Close:', e.reason);
153	          },
154	        },
155	        config: config,
156	      });
157	
158	      const inputTurns = 'Turn on the lights please';
159	      session.sendClientContent({ turns: inputTurns });
160	
161	      let turns = await handleTurn();
162	
163	      for (const turn of turns) {
164	        if (turn.toolCall) {
165	          console.debug('A tool was called');
166	          const functionResponses = [];
167	          for (const fc of turn.toolCall.functionCalls) {
168	            functionResponses.push({
169	              id: fc.id,
170	              name: fc.name,
171	              response: { result: "ok" } // simple, hard-coded function response
172	            });
173	          }
174	
175	          console.debug('Sending tool response...\n');
176	          session.sendToolResponse({ functionResponses: functionResponses });
177	        }
178	      }
179	
180	      // Check again for new messages
181	      turns = await handleTurn();
182	
183	      // Combine audio data strings and save as wave file
184	      const combinedAudio = turns.reduce((acc, turn) => {
185	          if (turn.data) {
186	              const buffer = Buffer.from(turn.data, 'base64');
187	              const intArray = new Int16Array(buffer.buffer, buffer.byteOffset, buffer.byteLength / Int16Array.BYTES_PER_ELEMENT);
188	              return acc.concat(Array.from(intArray));
189	          }
190	          return acc;
191	      }, []);
192	
193	      const audioBuffer = new Int16Array(combinedAudio);
194	
195	      const wf = new WaveFile();
196	      wf.fromScratch(1, 24000, '16', audioBuffer);  // output is 24kHz
197	      fs.writeFileSync('audio.wav', wf.toBuffer());
198	
199	      session.close();
200	    }
201	
202	    async function main() {
203	      await live().catch((e) => console.error('got error', e));
204	    }
205	
206	    main();
207	
208	From a single prompt, the model can generate multiple function calls and the
209	code necessary to chain their outputs. This code executes in a sandbox
210	environment, generating subsequent [BidiGenerateContentToolCall](https://ai.google.dev/api/live#bidigeneratecontenttoolcall) messages.
211	
212	## Asynchronous function calling
213	
214	Function calling executes sequentially by default, meaning execution pauses
215	until the results of each function call are available. This ensures sequential
216	processing, which means you won't be able to continue interacting with the model
217	while the functions are being run.
218	
219	> [!NOTE]
220	> **Note:** Asynchronous function calling is not yet supported in Gemini 3.1 Flash Live. The model will not start responding until you've sent the tool response.
221	
222	If you don't want to block the conversation, you can tell the model to run the
223	functions asynchronously. To do so, you first need to add a `behavior` to the
224	function definitions:
225	
226	### Python
227	
228	    # Non-blocking function definitions
229	    turn_on_the_lights = {"name": "turn_on_the_lights", "behavior": "NON_BLOCKING"} # turn_on_the_lights will run asynchronously
230	    turn_off_the_lights = {"name": "turn_off_the_lights"} # turn_off_the_lights will still pause all interactions with the model
231	
232	### JavaScript
233	
234	    import { GoogleGenAI, Modality, Behavior } from '@google/genai';
235	
236	    // Non-blocking function definitions
237	    const turn_on_the_lights = {name: "turn_on_the_lights", behavior: Behavior.NON_BLOCKING}
238	
239	    // Blocking function definitions
240	    const turn_off_the_lights = {name: "turn_off_the_lights"}
241	
242	    const tools = [{ functionDeclarations: [turn_on_the_lights, turn_off_the_lights] }]
243	
244	`NON-BLOCKING` ensures the function runs asynchronously while you can
245	continue interacting with the model.
246	
247	Then you need to tell the model how to behave when it receives the
248	`FunctionResponse` using the `scheduling` parameter. It can either:
249	
250	- Interrupt what it's doing and tell you about the response it got right away (`scheduling="INTERRUPT"`),
251	- Wait until it's finished with what it's currently doing (`scheduling="WHEN_IDLE"`),
252	- Or do nothing and use that knowledge later on in the discussion
253	  (`scheduling="SILENT"`)
254	
255	### Python
256	
257	    # for a non-blocking function definition, apply scheduling in the function response:
258	      function_response = types.FunctionResponse(
259	          id=fc.id,
260	          name=fc.name,
261	          response={
262	              "result": "ok",
263	              "scheduling": "INTERRUPT" # Can also be WHEN_IDLE or SILENT
264	          }
265	      )
266	
267	### JavaScript
268	
269	    import { GoogleGenAI, Modality, Behavior, FunctionResponseScheduling } from '@google/genai';
270	
271	    // for a non-blocking function definition, apply scheduling in the function response:
272	    const functionResponse = {
273	      id: fc.id,
274	      name: fc.name,
275	      response: {
276	        result: "ok",
277	        scheduling: FunctionResponseScheduling.INTERRUPT  // Can also be WHEN_IDLE or SILENT
278	      }
279	    }
280	
281	## Grounding with Google Search
282	
283	You can enable Grounding with Google Search as part of the session
284	configuration. This increases the Live API's accuracy and prevents
285	hallucinations. See the [Grounding tutorial](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/grounding) to
286	learn more.
287	
288	### Python
289	
290	    import asyncio
291	    import wave
292	    from google import genai
293	    from google.genai import types
294	
295	    client = genai.Client()
296	
297	    model = "gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview"
298	
299	    tools = [{'google_search': {}}]
300	    config = {"response_modalities": ["AUDIO"], "tools": tools}
301	
302	    async def main():
303	        async with client.aio.live.connect(model=model, config=config) as session:
304	            prompt = "When did the last Brazil vs. Argentina soccer match happen?"
305	            await session.send_client_content(turns={"parts": [{"text": prompt}]})
306	
307	            wf = wave.open("audio.wav", "wb")
308	            wf.setnchannels(1)
309	            wf.setsampwidth(2)
310	            wf.setframerate(24000)  # Output is 24kHz
311	
312	            async for chunk in session.receive():
313	                if chunk.server_content:
314	                    if chunk.data is not None:
315	                        wf.writeframes(chunk.data)
316	
317	                    # The model might generate and execute Python code to use Search
318	                    model_turn = chunk.server_content.model_turn
319	                    if model_turn:
320	                        for part in model_turn.parts:
321	                            if part.executable_code is not None:
322	                                print(part.executable_code.code)
323	
324	                            if part.code_execution_result is not None:
325	                                print(part.code_execution_result.output)
326	
327	            wf.close()
328	
329	    if __name__ == "__main__":
330	        asyncio.run(main())
331	
332	### JavaScript
333	
334	    import { GoogleGenAI, Modality } from '@google/genai';
335	    import * as fs from "node:fs";
336	    import pkg from 'wavefile';  // npm install wavefile
337	    const { WaveFile } = pkg;
338	
339	    const ai = new GoogleGenAI({});
340	    const model = 'gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview';
341	
342	    const tools = [{ googleSearch: {} }]
343	    const config = {
344	      responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO],
345	      tools: tools
346	    }
347	
348	    async function live() {
349	      const responseQueue = [];
350	
351	      async function waitMessage() {
352	        let done = false;
353	        let message = undefined;
354	        while (!done) {
355	          message = responseQueue.shift();
356	          if (message) {
357	            done = true;
358	          } else {
359	            await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
360	          }
361	        }
362	        return message;
363	      }
364	
365	      async function handleTurn() {
366	        const turns = [];
367	        let done = false;
368	        while (!done) {
369	          const message = await waitMessage();
370	          turns.push(message);
371	          if (message.serverContent && message.serverContent.turnComplete) {
372	            done = true;
373	          } else if (message.toolCall) {
374	            done = true;
375	          }
376	        }
377	        return turns;
378	      }
379	
380	      const session = await ai.live.connect({
381	        model: model,
382	        callbacks: {
383	          onopen: function () {
384	            console.debug('Opened');
385	          },
386	          onmessage: function (message) {
387	            responseQueue.push(message);
388	          },
389	          onerror: function (e) {
390	            console.debug('Error:', e.message);
391	          },
392	          onclose: function (e) {
393	            console.debug('Close:', e.reason);
394	          },
395	        },
396	        config: config,
397	      });
398	
399	      const inputTurns = 'When did the last Brazil vs. Argentina soccer match happen?';
400	      session.sendClientContent({ turns: inputTurns });
401	
402	      let turns = await handleTurn();
403	
404	      let combinedData = '';
405	      for (const turn of turns) {
406	        if (turn.serverContent && turn.serverContent.modelTurn && turn.serverContent.modelTurn.parts) {
407	          for (const part of turn.serverContent.modelTurn.parts) {
408	            if (part.executableCode) {
409	              console.debug('executableCode: %s\n', part.executableCode.code);
410	            }
411	            else if (part.codeExecutionResult) {
412	              console.debug('codeExecutionResult: %s\n', part.codeExecutionResult.output);
413	            }
414	            else if (part.inlineData && typeof part.inlineData.data === 'string') {
415	              combinedData += atob(part.inlineData.data);
416	            }
417	          }
418	        }
419	      }
420	
421	      // Convert the base64-encoded string of bytes into a Buffer.
422	      const buffer = Buffer.from(combinedData, 'binary');
423	
424	      // The buffer contains raw bytes. For 16-bit audio, we need to interpret every 2 bytes as a single sample.
425	      const intArray = new Int16Array(buffer.buffer, buffer.byteOffset, buffer.byteLength / Int16Array.BYTES_PER_ELEMENT);
426	
427	      const wf = new WaveFile();
428	      // The API returns 16-bit PCM audio at a 24kHz sample rate.
429	      wf.fromScratch(1, 24000, '16', intArray);
430	      fs.writeFileSync('audio.wav', wf.toBuffer());
431	
432	      session.close();
433	    }
434	
435	    async function main() {
436	      await live().catch((e) => console.error('got error', e));
437	    }
438	
439	    main();
440	
441	## Combining multiple tools
442	
443	You can combine multiple tools within the Live API,
444	increasing your application's capabilities even more:
445	
446	### Python
447	
448	    prompt = """
449	    Hey, I need you to do two things for me.
450	
451	    1. Use Google Search to look up information about the largest earthquake in California the week of Dec 5 2024?
452	    2. Then turn on the lights
453	
454	    Thanks!
455	    """
456	
457	    tools = [
458	        {"google_search": {}},
459	        {"function_declarations": [turn_on_the_lights, turn_off_the_lights]},
460	    ]
461	
462	    config = {"response_modalities": ["AUDIO"], "tools": tools}
463	
464	    # ... remaining model call
465	
466	### JavaScript
467	
468	    const prompt = `Hey, I need you to do two things for me.
469	
470	    1. Use Google Search to look up information about the largest earthquake in California the week of Dec 5 2024?
471	    2. Then turn on the lights
472	
473	    Thanks!
474	    `
475	
476	    const tools = [
